# Secrets — NEVER commit
.env
.env.*
# ...except the template, which holds only placeholders and is what
# alembic/env.py tells you to copy. Keep it that way: no real value here.
!.env.example
gshk/secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Local working folders — not part of the repo
PRD/
Wireframe/
docs/

# ...except a few things under the TOP-LEVEL docs/ that are INPUTS, not
# documentation. The leading slashes matter: `docs/` above matches at any
# depth, and backend/docs/ must STAY ignored — it holds the CR public key PEM,
# which is deliberately env-var-only in deployment (services/tpsi/config.py).
#
# CR's two worked specimens are the ground truth tests/test_nar1_field_map.py
# checks the NAR1 field map against. Without them in the repo those tests skip
# themselves in CI, and a silently-skipped verification is worse than none —
# the map would be unguarded while looking guarded.
#
# CR's blank form is NOT here: it is a RUNTIME asset and lives with the code
# that fills it, at backend/services/nar1_form/form/NAR1_fillable.pdf.
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/NAR1(private)_Specimen-e.pdf
!/docs/NAR1(public)_Specimen-e.pdf
!/docs/QUEUED.md
# The design spec for the NAR1 facsimile, because the code refers to it for
# WHY the field map looks the way it does. Deliberately this one file and not
# `!/docs/superpowers/` — that would sweep in every historical plan and spec
# under it (~12k lines of execution logs), which is a decision for Levi to
# make on purpose rather than a side effect of this one.
!/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/
/docs/superpowers/specs/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-30-nar1-form-facsimile-design.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
